{"answer":"There are 7 subsets. One is {1,8}. Exhaustively: a subset of sum 9 has at most three elements, since the smallest four distinct positive elements sum to 10. The two-element subsets are {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, and {4,5}; the three-element subsets are {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}. Thus 4+3=7.","approaches":[{"description":"Enumerate by subset cardinality, using the minimum possible sum for four distinct positive elements to bound the cardinality.","id":"cardinality-casework","outcome":"candidate","reason":"It lists every possible cardinality and solves each remaining distinct-sum case."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in steps bound-four through total-seven.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"count-seven","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Exactly 7 subsets of {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} have sum 9.","step_ids":["bound-four","pairs-list","triples-list","total-seven"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Established in step pairs-list.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"pair-count","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The two-element subsets with sum 9 are {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, and {4,5}.","step_ids":["pairs-list"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Established in step triples-list.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"triple-count","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The three-element subsets with sum 9 are {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}.","step_ids":["triples-list"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"bound-four","justification":"A subset has no repeated elements. Its four smallest possible elements are 1, 2, 3, and 4, whose sum is 10; hence a sum-9 subset has at most three elements. The empty set and every singleton have sum at most 8, so only sizes two and three remain.","statement":"Every subset of the given set with sum 9 has either two or three elements."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["bound-four"],"id":"pairs-list","justification":"For a two-element subset {a,b} with a<b and a+b=9, a can only be 1, 2, 3, or 4. The corresponding b=9-a gives exactly the four listed pairs.","statement":"The complete two-element list is {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["bound-four"],"id":"triples-list","justification":"Write a<b<c and a+b+c=9. If a=1, then b+c=8 with b<c, giving (b,c)=(2,6) or (3,5). If a=2, then b+c=7 with b>2 and b<c, giving (3,4). If a>=3, then a+b+c>=3+4+5=12, impossible.","statement":"The complete three-element list is {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, {2,3,4}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["pairs-list","triples-list"],"id":"total-seven","justification":"The exhaustive cases contain four and three subsets respectively, and subsets of different cardinalities are distinct.","statement":"The total number is 4+3=7."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
